   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Western Hemisphere Regional Migration Capacity Building Program (WHP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program aims to enhance the capacities of governments and key stakeholders to improve migration governance, ensuring safe, orderly, and regular migration while reducing vulnerabilities of migrants. It aligns with IOM&apos;s strategic vision and regional strategy for 2020-2024 in North America, Central America, and the Caribbean. The program adopts a comprehensive approach, focusing on capacity-building in program countries for effective migration management, partnerships, crisis response, and communication. Following IOM&apos;s &quot;Rights Based Approach to Programming Manual,&quot; the program integrates a rights-based and gender-sensitive perspective in all activities, emphasizing migrants&apos; rights throughout the project cycle. Additionally, IOM&apos;s Migration Governance Framework emphasizes conforming to international standards and safeguarding migrants&apos; rights for humane and organized migration that benefits both migrants and society. Thus, in program implementation, IOM places significant importance on recognizing and safeguarding the rights of migrants, regardless of nationality or migration status, and ensuring that these rights are upheld and fulfilled by States, while also promoting migrants&apos; awareness of their rights.</narrative>
  </description>
